      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_753c1e6661560b20f0b962a1b6cc3be3b4d4163c45749f8c86838079ff683dc1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Arithmetic evaluation and period identities create an observable-specific translation ladder: truncated Eisenstein series supply locally normalized test states, CM-point and Shimura-Waldspurger formulas convert pointwise size into degree-two L-value growth, and Rankin-Selberg periods convert mass against Eisenstein tests into degree-four central values for which a subconvex saving yields individual equidistribution.",
